\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textcolor {teal}{Share of outputs that pass compilation or another well-formedness check (gray) and share that pass the behavioral check (blue) in the 18 papers that report both for the same outputs. Numbers on the right give the gap in percentage points. Each row shows the configuration in parentheses or otherwise the paper's own system; the RISE and DepWareTrans rows are baselines, the DepTrans row is an ablation and the BatFix row shows the translations before repair. Rates are as reported or computed from reported counts, except that DepUpgrade and IntentTester report the behavioral rate over the outputs that compile and we recompute it over all outputs. The behavioral check differs by paper (DepUpgrade uses human review, IntentTester's outputs are tests and ReCodeAgent counts passing tests rather than programs), so a gap is meaningful only within its row. The replication package lists each configuration and where the paper reports it.}}}{13}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:compile-gap}{{3}{13}{\new {Share of outputs that pass compilation or another well-formedness check (gray) and share that pass the behavioral check (blue) in the 18 papers that report both for the same outputs. Numbers on the right give the gap in percentage points. Each row shows the configuration in parentheses or otherwise the paper's own system; the RISE and DepWareTrans rows are baselines, the DepTrans row is an ablation and the BatFix row shows the translations before repair. Rates are as reported or computed from reported counts, except that DepUpgrade and IntentTester report the behavioral rate over the outputs that compile and we recompute it over all outputs. The behavioral check differs by paper (DepUpgrade uses human review, IntentTester's outputs are tests and ReCodeAgent counts passing tests rather than programs), so a gap is meaningful only within its row. The replication package lists each configuration and where the paper reports it.}}{figure.caption.25}{}}
